@* The application and its user interface.
The class |App| owns the renderer and the material library, holds the state that the
user can change, and builds the user interface every frame. The interface is made with
Dear ImGui, an \emph{immediate-mode} library: there are no widget objects to create and
destroy; every frame, the program simply calls |ImGui::Button|, |ImGui::SliderFloat| and so
on, and each call both draws the widget and reports whether the user interacted with it.
This style fits a teaching tool very well, because the state lives in plain variables
that the rest of the program reads directly.

