@ \label{probestate}The state of the probe deserves attention. The probe follows the
mouse while it hovers any map; a left click \emph{pins} it, so that the user can then
move the mouse elsewhere---to rotate the camera, say---while the readouts stay. The flag
|hoveredThisFrame_| is cleared at the start of each frame and set by any map image that
the mouse is over; at the end of the interface, an unpinned probe that nobody hovered
becomes invalid.

<<State of the inspector>>=
// Inspector
MapKind inspected_ = MapColor;
bool hoveredThisFrame_ = false, pinned_ = false;
DirectX::XMFLOAT2 probeUV_{0.5f, 0.5f};
bool probeValid_ = false;
HoverInfo info_;

